Minecraft Dungeons II: Native Controller Prompts
{{LABEL}}

Dungeons II shows Xbox button prompts to everyone on PC. This makes it show
{{LABEL}} ones instead.

It does not replace any artwork. The game already ships these icons in the
Windows build, it just never picks them. This is a two line config file that
tells it to.


INSTALL, pick either one

  A) Right-click Start, open Terminal, paste this, press Enter:

{{ONELINER}}

  B) Or copy Game.ini into this folder yourself:

       %LOCALAPPDATA%\Dungeons2\Saved\Config\Windows

     Microsoft Store and Game Pass use this one instead:

       %LOCALAPPDATA%\Packages\Microsoft.MinecraftDungeons2_8wekyb3d8bbwe\LocalCache\Local\Dungeons2\Saved\Config\Windows

     Paste the path into the Explorer address bar and it will take you
     there. If a Game.ini is already sitting in that folder, add these two
     lines to the end of it rather than replacing the file:

       [CommonInputPlatformSettings_Windows CommonInputPlatformSettings]
       DefaultGamepadName={{GAMEPAD}}

     Then right-click that file, open Properties, and tick Read-only. Do
     not skip it, see below.

Either way, restart the game afterwards.


WHY READ-ONLY?

The game rewrites its own user config when it shuts down, keeping only the
values it believes it owns. Ours is not one of them, so on a clean exit it
deletes the file and you are back to Xbox prompts next time you play.

Marking it read-only stops that. The game still reads the setting on
startup, then finds it cannot write the file back and carries on. Nothing
of yours lives in that file. Your graphics and audio settings are in
GameUserSettings.ini next to it and stay writable.

The one line installer above does this for you.


UNINSTALL

Delete that Game.ini. Windows asks you to confirm because the file is
read-only, which is expected. That is all of it. Nothing else was touched.


NO PROMPTS AT ALL?

Then your controller is not reaching the game and this mod has nothing to
relabel. Check that the pad is actually awake, since one that is paired over
Bluetooth but asleep still shows up in Windows while being invisible to the
game. Toggling Steam Input for the game is worth a try too.


NOTES

Cosmetic only, so it is safe in multiplayer. It lives in your user config
rather than the game's data, so a patch should not wipe it. Built against
Dungeons II 1.1.1.0 on Unreal Engine 5.6.1.

Other versions of this are up for DualSense, DualShock 4, Switch and Xbox
Series controllers.
